Terraform

Terraform is an Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool created by HashiCorp.

Instead of manually creating AWS resources through the AWS Console, you write configuration code that tells AWS what infrastructure you want.

Without Terraform

You manually do:

AWS Console
   ↓
Create S3 bucket
   ↓
Create IAM role
   ↓
Create EC2
   ↓
Configure networking
   ↓
Create SageMaker resources

This can take a lot of clicking and can lead to mistakes.

With Terraform

You write Terraform configuration:

Terraform Code
      ↓
Terraform
      ↓
AWS
      ↓
S3 + IAM + EC2 + VPC + SageMaker

Terraform creates the resources automatically.

Simple example

For example, you can tell Terraform:

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "insurance_data" {
  bucket = "my-insurance-data-bucket"
}

Then Terraform can create that S3 bucket in AWS.

The important commands are:

terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply

terraform init → prepares Terraform.

terraform plan → shows what Terraform is going to create/change.

terraform apply → actually creates/changes the AWS resources.

And:

terraform destroy

→ removes the infrastructure that Terraform manages.
